WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.660
- We're back and our next guest is one

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.490
of the foremost leaders
in the world of fashion.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.740
She's been part of Forbes,
Most Powerful Women,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.250
Time's, Most Influential

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.500
and was inducted into The
National Women's Hall of Fame.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.490
Her new book is called "Own
it, The secret to life."

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.540
It's out on March 8th

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.513
everybody please welcome
Diane Von Furstenberg.

00:00:19.398 --> 00:00:24.200
(audience clapping)
(soft music)

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.210
Well hello, nice to see you.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.200
Yeah, I see it.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.890
You know what I see also, your love,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.680
that would be my favorite
room in your house.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.550
I love a library.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.160
Is that your office or a library?

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.170
- It is my studio.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.800
I have actually been, I'm in the country

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.250
and I have been here in
this room for a year now.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.083
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.730
- But it's a good room to be stuck in.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.010
- I love that room.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.240
It's inspiring.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.073
I saw it and I was like,

00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:51.720
"Oh I wanna just read
and get lost in there."

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.330
- Come, come.
- And by the way,

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.520
my favorite color is green.
- I know.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.743
- And this is your dress.
- I know, I know.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.210
You look great with leopards all over you.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.760
- I feel like I do too, Diane.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.650
So now, I love it.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.050
I love your wrap dress,
these are my favorite

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.250
but I love green, is
also my favorite color.

00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:14.070
I just learned that you
do something awesome

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.350
with emails every morning.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.530
Can you tell everybody what you do?

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:22.530
- Well, what I try to do
is I try to every morning

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.260
to use my magic wand, which
means that with my email

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:35.091
I pick, I do one big email

00:01:35.091 --> 00:01:38.090
that totally does not benefit me.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.690
So I may introduce somebody to somebody

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.110
that they would never have met

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:48.340
and you could actually
change someone's life.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.610
So I do that.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.990
And it's very interesting because

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.390
the more you use your magic wand,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.440
the more powerful your magic wand is.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.840
But very often your magic
wand comes right back to you.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.430
And it becomes a boomerang

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.510
- I've never heard of anyone doing that.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.740
And it's so, it's such an
obvious, cool thing to do.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.390
- It's such a good thing to do.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.690
And the reason I like to talk about it

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.180
because people get inspired
and then they do it

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.570
but you have to do it with care.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.830
- I wanted to talk about that.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.600
'Cause I want people to hear that

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.660
and possibly implement
that in their lives.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.700
'Cause that kind of
networking is so beautiful

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.830
and those connections are so wonderful.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.620
But I got to talk about your book though,

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.230
because you you held it up for us

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.420
and the title of your book is "Own It."

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.033
So what does owning it mean to you?

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.273
- All right,

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.323
first of all, when people asked me,

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.694
"What did you wanna do when you-",

00:02:48.694 --> 00:02:51.210
well, I said I didn't
know what I wanted to do

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.060
but I knew the kind of
woman I wanted to be.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.690
I wanted to be a woman in charge.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.930
Then people would say, "Who do you dress?"

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.450
And I would say, "The woman in charge."

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.510
And then I realized that to be in charge

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.450
may sound aggressive, but
really it's not aggressive.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.820
To be in charge is to be who you are,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.680
is owning who you are.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:18.980
You only perfect your imperfection,
they become your asset.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.600
You own your vulnerability.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.250
It becomes your strength.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.800
And so I decided to
write this little guide

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.690
it's really a guide, "Own It"

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.850
because owning it is the secret to life.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.360
And then the minute you own
it, you already deal with it.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.130
- Yeah, I love all of that

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.370
but Diane said she loves connecting people

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.300
and we have an amazing young woman

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.630
hoping to change the
world through medicine.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:51.260
So would you be up for,
I don't know, connecting?

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.463
Can I connect her with you?

00:03:52.463 --> 00:03:53.320
- I would love them.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.400
- I wanna play fairy godmother today.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.750
I wanna (giggles),

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.220
well, I'm gonna hide Diane.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.400
- I play godmother every day.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.610
- I think that's a beautiful thing.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.600
- As you do too.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.433
- I am very fortunate.

00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.806
I have a lot of people here
helping me with my wand.

00:04:09.806 --> 00:04:12.670
So it's amazing what you're
doing all on your own

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.640
with your emails.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.670
But we're gonna hide Diane
in our virtual green room

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.090
and bring her back to surprise
a very promising young woman.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:20.923
I'm back,

00:04:20.923 --> 00:04:23.920
and my next guest is nothing
short of extraordinary.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.110
She's a high school senior

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.650
whose goal is to be a neurosurgeon.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.300
That's crazy.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.680
She recently got accepted
to her dream school

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.570
Barnard College in New York city.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.110
But when her family fell
in hard financial times

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.480
she actually used the money
she'd saved for college

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.230
to pay her mom's rent,
which makes her amazing.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.704
Everybody let's welcome Alondra.

00:04:43.704 --> 00:04:46.760
(clapping)

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.380
So Alondra, I mean,

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.070
we already know you have a heart of gold

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.000
from what I just said

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.290
but also congratulations on
getting into Barnard college.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.460
That's amazing.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.090
- Thank you so much,
Barnard is my dream school.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.990
I just can't believe I got in.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.100
- Oh my God, it's insane.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.180
And you, I heard you paid your mom's rent

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.730
with what you've saved for school, right?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:10.170
But you still manage to
pay for Barnard, right?

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.100
What happened.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.040
- Yeah, so last year in February,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.290
my mom she broke her ankle

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.970
and I know it was gonna be hard for her

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.310
to get some hours back.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.880
And that was when I just broke down

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.300
because I had done everything right.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.480
I got into my dream school
and now I just, I couldn't go.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.390
And that was so heartbreaking

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.750
because I knew I had to work so hard

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.710
and now it's just my
dream has to stop here.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.933
And it was basically like,
I can't go to Barnard.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.590
Nothing can happen from here.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.160
And so I had been thinking
of making a Go-fund Me

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:45.320
and I told my mom, okay,
you can have my savings.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.210
I told her, we can make up
the money that I gave you.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.930
And so she took it from me
and she was a bit hesitant

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.790
but I knew she needed the help.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.135
And then about four days later

00:05:56.135 --> 00:05:56.968
I started getting traction,

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:58.840
all the media outlets,
they started sharing it.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.240
And I was just so excited

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.453
because everyone was
showing so much stuff.

00:06:03.453 --> 00:06:05.730
All the love, we're just so happy.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:06.980
- What an amazing,

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.250
I think that's karma
working at its finest.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.230
Like you did something beautiful

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.900
and from your heart and really
was hard for you probably,

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.033
you saved that money

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:17.050
for something that was important to you.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.810
And then you set this whole thing up

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.480
and look at the universe,
look at God, just giving back.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.630
That's such a beautiful thing.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.120
Well, New York is a big place.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.890
It's a huge, they call
it the Big Apple, right?

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.150
So it probably wouldn't hurt

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.810
to have some good connections there.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.540
So Alondra, I wanna
introduce you to someone

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.000
if that's all right.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.910
She basically knows
everybody who's anybody.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.160
She's a business mogul, a fashion designer

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.620
an author and an all around icon.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.411
What I'm saying is she's a
whole lotta woman, Alondra.

00:06:46.411 --> 00:06:48.994
(upbeat music)

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.657
All right Alondra meet,
Diane Von Furstenberg.

00:06:55.653 --> 00:06:59.653
(audience clapping)
She laughed.

00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:02.730
- Hi.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.600
- I love that she-
- Hi, so nice to meet you.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.450
- She giggled like a total
score, it was awesome.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:14.450
- Hello, welcome to Barnard
and welcome to New York.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.160
- Diane is all about
connecting people, Alondra.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.510
And she's just really good at
connecting people she knows

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:22.300
with people who don't know each other.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.470
And the hope is that they
can support one another.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:27.140
So we wanna do the same, so Diane,

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.720
what advice do you have for Alondra?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.553
- All right.

00:07:30.553 --> 00:07:31.990
So Alondra,

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.680
when you arrive in a new
place like New York city

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.570
it's kind of nice to know
that you have a godmother.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.980
It's kind of nice to know
that if anything goes wrong

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.540
or not you can always call on someone.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:54.850
And so I want you to know
that while you are in college

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:58.433
you can call me anytime for anything.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:02.190
- Thank you so much.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.720
- Alondra, I wish you nothing but success.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.860
And I know that Diane can
help you in any way you want.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.830
And she's just like a
little fairy godmother

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.580
when it comes to networking.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:13.110
And I'm just so proud of you.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.660
I don't know you until now,

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.570
but I'm so proud of you like
to have big dreams like that

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.400
and really go for it is an
accomplishment in itself

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.700
because it can be a scary thing

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.200
and especially moving
to a different place.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.280
And I'm just super excited for you, okay.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.080
- I still can't believe I'm even on here.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.300
It's just crazy.
(Kelly giggles)

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.970
I was literally crying a week ago

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.500
because I couldn't pay for college.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:34.900
And now I'm on show,

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.470
gonna be able to go to my dream school

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.620
and I have a mentor.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.920
Oh, I'm so excited.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.110
- I'm telling you what,
if you're a good person,

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.750
I think things can happen.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.793
- Dream come true.

